        "original_id": "e54891a0-e4c3-5217-b7c6-5a2f744ef023",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, William Rotko, Robert Hanssen, Eric O'Neill\n- Works: Breach\n- Organizations: FBI, Soviet intelligence, Russian intelligence\n- Topics: espionage, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Hanssen was born on April 18, 1944.\n- From 1979 to 2001, Robert Hanssen was an FBI agent who spied against the United States for Soviet and Russian intelligence services for 22 years.\n- Eric O'Neill worked as Robert Hanssen's assistant and helped bring about Robert Hanssen's downfall.\n- Robert Hanssen was later convicted of spying for the Soviet Union and later Russia.\n- In 2007, Breach was released as an American historical and political thriller film.\n- Billy Ray directed Breach.\n- Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, and William Rotko wrote the screenplay for Breach.\n- The screenplay for Breach is based on the true story of Robert Hanssen and Eric O'Neill.",
